st run, and lost only one-thousandth in the next one, leading them to their expected gold medal. Behind them, their club mates " [:a {:href "/athletes/83964"} "Behrendt"] "/" [:a {:href "/athletes/88609"} "Krauße"] " slid to a surprising silver medal, not having previous experience at major championships. As usual, the two-run doubles competition was close, especially the battle for bronze. " [:a {:href "/athletes/83983"} "Belyakov"] "/" [:a {:href "/athletes/83982"} "Belousov"] " (URS) who were leading the World Cup standings, were in bronze medal position after one run, but tumbled to seventh with a disappointing second run. The West German duo " [:a {:href "/athletes/97341"} "Schwab"] "/" [:a {:href "/athletes/97780"} "Wolfgang"] " was able to benefit from this mishap, and despite only placing 5th in the second run they moved from fourth to third."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Run #1"] [:th {} "Run #2"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/86702"} "Jörg Hoffmann"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/96437"} "Jochen Pietzsch"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "1:31.940"] [:td {} "45.786 (1)"] [:td {} "46.154 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/88609"} "Stefan Krauße"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/83964"} "Jan Behrendt"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "1:32.039"] [:td {} "45.886 (2)"] [:td {} "46.153 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [: